course: dictionary
lesson: 194
title: Airtight: sealed shut
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Airtight is two words joined: air and tight. Something airtight is sealed so well that no air can get in or out. «Silage is grass wrapped up airtight so bacteria turn its sugars into acid and pickle it.» The wrapping is sealed, so air stays out and the grass keeps fresh for months.
explain: Airtight can also describe an argument. «An airtight alibi» proves that a suspect could not have done a crime. The clue is the idea of no gaps: an airtight case has no weak points, so nobody can prove it wrong.
explain: «The air will not run out, because lifts are not airtight.» This sentence is about air moving. A lift is not sealed, so air can get in and out. The clue is the word not: if something is not airtight, air can get through it.
fact: Airtight means sealed so tightly that no air can get in or out.
fact: Airtight can also mean an argument, alibi or case with no weak points.
fact: Airtight containers keep food fresh and stop it going stale or mouldy.
fact: In science, airtight containers show that things need air to burn or rot.
fact: Phrases to know: airtight container, airtight seal, airtight alibi.
exercise: «Silage is grass wrapped up airtight so bacteria turn its sugars into acid.» What does airtight mean here? | Very cold and frozen | *Sealed so no air can get in or out | Made of plastic that floats | Loose and open to the breeze
exercise: Why can air move in and out of a lift? | Because lifts are made of gold | Because lifts are always painted white | *Because a lift is not sealed
exercise: «An airtight alibi» in a detective story proves what? | *The suspect could not have done the crime | The suspect has a loose seal | The suspect was very hungry
test: Which of these would be airtight? | A torn paper bag | An open window | A net curtain | *A jar with a lid pressed on tight
test: An airtight argument means it has what? | *No weak points | Lots of pictures | Very short sentences | Very loud words
exam: Which sentence uses airtight correctly? | *The jar was airtight, so the biscuits stayed crisp | My sandwich is airtight with a big smile | The sky was airtight and full of stars | The river was airtight after the rain
